From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomonori Nakagawa <jack@supremeoverlordjabs.co>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 22:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] sprdwcn: do not latch the firmware-partition fallback on a
 missing blob

marlin_download_from_file() and gnss_download_from_file() try
request_firmware() once and, on failure, set is_btwf_in_sysfs /
is_gnss_in_sysfs and switch permanently to *_download_from_partition(),
which reads the Android firmware partition by block-device path.

On this board the WCN core is built in (CONFIG_UNISOC_WCN_BSP=y) and
probes from the initramfs, where wcnmodem.bin is deliberately absent so
that marlin does not spend a minute bringing the chip up while udev is
still settling. That first, expected failure latched the flag, so when
sc23xx_wlan_sdio loaded after switch_root and called start_marlin() the
firmware on the rootfs was never looked at:

  WCN BASEno find wcnmodem.bin errno:(-2)(ignore!!)
  ...
  WCN BASEmarlin download timeout
  sc23xx-wlan-sdio sprd-marlin3:wlan: failed to power on WCN: -1

There is no Android firmware partition here, so the fallback can never
succeed. Fail the current attempt and leave the flag alone, so the next
start_marlin() goes through request_firmware() again.

Signed-off-by: Tomonori Nakagawa <jack@supremeoverlordjabs.co>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/sprdwcn/platform/wcn_boot.c | 20 ++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/sprdwcn/platform/wcn_boot.c	2026-09-02 22:35:28
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/sprdwcn/platform/wcn_boot.c	2026-09-02 22:35:28
@@ -882,11 +882,13 @@
 	err = request_firmware(&firmware, "gnssmodem.bin", NULL);
 #endif
 	if (err < 0) {
+		/*
+		 * No Android firmware partition on this board: don't latch
+		 * is_gnss_in_sysfs, so a later attempt (after the rootfs is
+		 * mounted) goes through request_firmware() again.
+		 */
 		pr_err("%s no find gnssmodem.bin err:%d(ignore)\n",
 			__func__, err);
-		marlin_dev->is_gnss_in_sysfs = true;
-		err = gnss_download_from_partition();
-
 		return err;
 	}
 
@@ -980,10 +982,16 @@
 	err = request_firmware(&firmware, "wcnmodem.bin", NULL);
 #endif
 	if (err < 0) {
+		/*
+		 * The built-in WCN core probes from the initramfs, where
+		 * wcnmodem.bin is deliberately absent. Latching
+		 * is_btwf_in_sysfs here would pin every later start_marlin()
+		 * to marlin_download_from_partition(), which cannot succeed
+		 * without the Android firmware partition, and Wi-Fi would stay
+		 * dead after the rootfs (and the firmware) shows up. Fail this
+		 * attempt only.
+		 */
 		pr_err("no find wcnmodem.bin errno:(%d)(ignore!!)\n", err);
-		marlin_dev->is_btwf_in_sysfs = true;
-		err = marlin_download_from_partition();
-
 		return err;
 	}
 
